            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            over the point.
          %h1#details Details
          %p
            Let
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SDiff"} SDiff
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
          %p
            We will define a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered category
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SDiff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SDiff
            called
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E Bord_{2|1}
            whose morphisms are smooth families of (2|1)-dimensional
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-cobordism"} super-cobordism
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi sTV
                    %mi fam
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sTV^{fam}
            of topological super vector bundles.
          %p So recall
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry+-+contents"}> supergeometry
              \.
          %p
            %strong> question
            \: What is the right notion of Riemannian or Euclidean structure on
            = succeed "s?" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-cobordism"} super-cobordism
          %p
            %strong> strategy
            \: From the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            perspective we need some structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            such that the “space” of maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(\Sigma,X)
            naturally carries some measure that allows to perform a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
          %p
            This perspective suggests certain generalizations of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
          %p
            We want to define
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+supermanifold"} Euclidean supermanifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            with
            %em flat
            Riemannian metric.
          %p notice that there is a canonical bijection between
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                flat
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
                = succeed "-dimensional" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %li
              %p
                a maximal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                consisting of charts such that all transition functions belong the the
                %strong Euclidean group
                or
                %strong Galileo group
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Eucl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo ⋊
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Eucl(\mathbb{R}^d)
                      \:=
                      \\mathbb{R}^d \rtimes O(\mathbb{R}^d)
              %p (rigid translations and rotations)
          %p In analogy to that we define:
          %p
            Similarly a
            %strong Euclidean structure
            on a
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d|\delta)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            is defined using the Euclidean
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+group"} super Lie group
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product"} semidirect product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Eucl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi δ
                  %mo ⋊
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Eucl(\mathbb{R}^{d|\delta})
                  \:=
                  \\mathbb{R}^{d|\delta}
                  \\rtimes
                  Spin(\mathbb{R}^d)
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin"} Spin
            group acts on the translations in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d|\delta}
            in a way to be specified.
          %p first recall the notion of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+supermanifold"} complex supermanifold
          %p
            %strong goal
            replace the standard Euclidean group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Eucl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R}^d, Eucl(\mathbb{R}^d))
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Euclidean+group"} super Euclidean group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,G)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a suitable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+group"} super Lie group
          %p This leads to the notion of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+supermanifold"}> Euclidean supermanifold
              \.
          %p
            The morphisms of the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E Bord_{(2|1)}
            will be
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+supermanifold"} Euclidean supermanifold
          %p
            %strong goal
            define the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Bord
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi δ
                            %mi sfam
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi cSDiff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  E Bord_{d|\delta}^{sfam}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow
                  \\\
                  cSDiff
                  }
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cSDiff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cSDiff
            is the category of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+supermanifold"} complex supermanifold
          %p The objects of this fibered category are
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ±
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %mo ←
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Y
                            %mi c
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Y^{\pm} &amp;\to&amp; Y &amp;\leftarrow&amp; Y^c
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp; \downarrow &amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; S
                  }
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to S
            is a family of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+supermanifold"} Euclidean supermanifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d|\delta)
          %p
            For the non-super, non-family version of
            %strong Euclidean bordism
            we require that the core
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^c
